module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.Regular

/-!
# Regular ideal sheaves

Let `X` be a ringed space and let `J ⊆ O_X` be a sheaf of ideals, realised as a submodule of
the rank-one structure sheaf module.  A finite family of sections `f₁, …, f_r` over an open `U`
is a *regular sequence* on `U` when, for each `i`, multiplication by `fᵢ` on
`O_X|_U / (f₁, …, f_{i-1})` is a monomorphism;  the quotient sheaf and that multiplication are
the data of Stacks tag 0639.  The ideal sheaf `J` is *regular* when near every point of the
support of `O_X / J` it is generated by such a sequence.

This is part (1) of Stacks tag 063D.  Both predicates,
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsRegularSequenceOn` and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsRegularIdealSheaf`, are defined in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RegularIdealSheaf/Regular.lean` together with parts (2) and
(3), Koszul-regularity and `H₁`-regularity; part (4), quasi-regularity, is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.IsQuasiRegularIdealSheaf` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RegularIdealSheaf/Basic.lean`, and the vocabulary of
generation on an open set is there as well.  This file re-exports the two predicates and adds
the local-witness restatement of the regular condition.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isRegularIdealSheaf_iff`: the definition of a
  regular ideal sheaf, restated as its local-witness form.

## Implementation notes

The quotient `O_X|_U / (f₁, …, f_{i-1})` and multiplication by `fᵢ` on it are taken from
`AlgebraicGeometry.regularSequenceMultiplication`, the library's form of Stacks tag 0639, which
is stated for *global* sections of a ringed space;  the sections over `U` are therefore turned
into global sections of the restriction `X|_U` by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionOnRestriction`, exactly as the
quasi-regular condition of part (4) does.

The multiplication map lives in the functor category of presheaves of abelian groups on `U`,
so `Mono` there is sectionwise injectivity;  since the quotient is a sheaf, that is equivalent
to injectivity on every stalk, which is how the source reads the condition (see the proof of
Stacks tag 063C).  No such stalk criterion is proved here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.20.1 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0639](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0639)
* [SGA 6, Exposé VII, Definition 1.4]
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular
open Stacks.RingedSpace

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

universe u

/-- Local-witness characterization of a regular ideal sheaf. -/
theorem isRegularIdealSheaf_iff (X : RingedSpace.{u})
    (J : (structureSheafModule X).Submodule) :
    IsRegularIdealSheaf X J ↔
      ∀ x : X, x ∈ idealQuotientSupport X J →
        ∃ (U : Opens X) (_hx : x ∈ U) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → X.presheaf.obj (op U)),
          IsRegularSequenceOn X U f ∧ IsGeneratedByOn X J U f :=
  Iff.rfl

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
